, and a fixed point is a self-loop. Also called a successor graph.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FunctionalGraph"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Following any vertex’s edges eventually repeats, so each weakly connected component holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly one cycle, with rooted trees hanging off its vertices (Flajolet and Odlyzko, “Random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mapping statistics”, EUROCRYPT ’89). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cycleDecomposition()"},{"type":"text","text":" finds every cycle and tree in O(n);"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successor(of:steps:)"},{"type":"text","text":" answers f^k(v) for any k."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For f given as a closure over a state space too large to store, use "},{"code":"floydCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"brentCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which need only "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" states and O(1) memory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph stores one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" per vertex, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f(v)"},{"type":"text","text":". The edge leaving "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" has position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},